WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.990
Northern Europe, 1315.

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:06.290
It rains, and keeps on raining.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:09.070
Harvests fail; winters are hard.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.950
People die of hunger on a scale remembered for centuries.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.310
Jump forward almost three hundred years, to a painting of a frozen canal.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.450
Hundreds of people are out on the ice.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.410
Two scenes from the same cold centuries.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.590
One looks like a catastrophe.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.930
The other looks like a holiday.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:31.150
Was the cold a disaster or did people adapt?

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.870
In this mission, you'll hear what one historian says caused the Great Famine.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.710
You'll read one more entry from Evelyn's diary, and look closely at that painting.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:45.790
Your mission: decide whether the cold was a disaster, or whether people adapted.
